codex
1. The incrementality defense is plausible but not yet reviewer-proof. Strongest objection: PaRC looks like PRP-Sorting/active PRP plus BT/Elo smoothing and a base-ranker interpolation. [PRP](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.17563) already uses symmetrized pairwise LLM comparisons, O(N log N) sorting, and fallback to initial ranking; recent active-PRP work explicitly targets noisy, order-sensitive, intransitive LLM comparisons. The text partially rebuts this via “anchored comparative residual” and λ=0 floor, but not enough: it must say why β is not merely BT strengths reparameterized around pony, and what identifying constraint makes “residual” real.

2. Citation issues/missing neighbors:
RankGPT and PRP are appropriate neighbors, but both are IR/document-ranking, not recommendation. You need rec-specific LLM ranking/reranking citations such as [LLMRank / Large Language Models are Zero-Shot Rankers for Recommender Systems](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.08845) and [LLM4Rerank](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.12433).
BT/Thurstone citations are appropriate, but missing Zermelo/Elo/Plackett-Luce/ranking-from-comparisons and active ranking-from-pairwise-comparisons.
Zheng et al. [LLM-as-a-Judge](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.05685) is appropriate for position/verbosity/self-enhancement bias, but it is weak support for “intransitive”; PRP supports order sensitivity, not necessarily cyclic intransitivity. Add direct intransitivity/preference-cycle citations.
“BT representation theorem” is over-formalized and likely mispositioned. Say scalar BT utilities cannot represent significant cyclic pairwise marginals, with a proper stochastic-transitivity/social-choice citation.
The “citation-audit, 2026-06-20” date is suspicious if this is being reviewed before that date.

3. Novelty framing is mostly restrained and better than typical overclaiming: “not absent from any conceivable pointwise scorer” is a good limitation. But “cannot underperform by construction” is too strong: λ=0 is in the validation search space, so the class contains the anchor; finite validation selection does not guarantee test non-degradation.

SCORE_POSITIONING: 7/10

Single most important fix: explicitly distinguish PaRC from PRP-Sorting/active PRP by defining β’s anchored-residual identifiability and adding the missing rec-specific and pairwise-comparison citations.
